write leaves plain sharing alone => "((1 2) (1 2))"
write-shared labels it => "(#0=(1 2) #0#)"
write-simple leaves it alone => "((1 2) (1 2))"
write labels a cycle => "#0=#(#0# 2)"
write-shared labels a cycle => "#0=#(#0# 2)"
write leaves a shared tail alone => "((1 3 4) (2 3 4))"
write-shared opens the spine => "((1 . #0=(3 4)) (2 . #0#))"
equal? still works after a scan => #t
and interleaved with write-shared => #t
